WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.916 --> 00:00:30.750
In the previous verse,

2
00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:32.208
Lord Krishna said

3
00:00:32.208 --> 00:00:34.958
that among humans, jñānī are the best.

4
00:00:34.958 --> 00:00:38.916
I am dear to them and they to Me.

5
00:00:38.916 --> 00:00:41.458
Now a natural question

6
00:00:41.458 --> 00:00:42.458
or concern

7
00:00:42.458 --> 00:00:43.833
may arise in the mind -

8
00:00:43.833 --> 00:00:46.375
the other three categories of ārta, arthārthī,

9
00:00:46.375 --> 00:00:49.666
and jijñāsu,

10
00:00:49.666 --> 00:00:51.625
are they not good?

11
00:00:51.625 --> 00:00:55.916
After all, many of us are in those very categories.

12
00:00:55.916 --> 00:00:58.666
In this verse, Lord Krishna

13
00:00:58.666 --> 00:01:01.291
is addressing this very concern or question.

14
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.583
At the very beginning of this verse, Lord Krishna

15
00:01:08.583 --> 00:01:12.291
clarifies that all four types of people

16
00:01:12.291 --> 00:01:15.875
who move toward Him are noble,

17
00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:16.916
excellent.

18
00:01:16.916 --> 00:01:18.750
We learned these four categories

19
00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:21.166
in the sixteenth verse -

20
00:01:21.166 --> 00:01:24.750
Ārta - who come to Krishna's shelter

21
00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:26.916
for removal of their sorrows,

22
00:01:26.916 --> 00:01:29.500
Arthārthī - who come

23
00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:33.000
because of desire for wealth/property,

24
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.125
Jijñāsu - who are curious to know 
the truth of life/soul

25
00:01:36.125 --> 00:01:38.875
and Krishna,

26
00:01:38.875 --> 00:01:42.333
and Jñānī - who are stable in this knowledge

27
00:01:42.333 --> 00:01:46.708
that Krishna is the supreme truth.

28
00:01:46.708 --> 00:01:50.750
Whatever the reason may be, all
 these come to Krishna's shelter,

29
00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:54.375
and Krishna considers all who
 come to His shelter as dear,

30
00:01:54.375 --> 00:01:56.250
accepts their devotion,

31
00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:58.166
is pleased with them.

32
00:01:58.166 --> 00:02:02.875
This very thing Krishna says shows
 His compassion and mercy.

33
00:02:02.875 --> 00:02:04.166
Even if

34
00:02:04.166 --> 00:02:06.250
personal desire is hidden behind devotion,

35
00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:08.625
Krishna still accepts it.

36
00:02:08.625 --> 00:02:10.333
His heart is vast,

37
00:02:10.333 --> 00:02:13.458
which embraces every surrendered one.

38
00:02:13.458 --> 00:02:15.125
But then,

39
00:02:15.125 --> 00:02:18.333
explaining what was said in
 the seventeenth verse,

40
00:02:18.333 --> 00:02:21.791
Krishna also says again that a jñānī,

41
00:02:21.791 --> 00:02:23.250
whose relationship with Krishna

42
00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:25.291
is completely selfless,

43
00:02:25.291 --> 00:02:27.541
is only of devotion and surrender,

44
00:02:27.541 --> 00:02:30.041
they consider them as their own form.

45
00:02:30.041 --> 00:02:31.125
They say,

46
00:02:31.125 --> 00:02:34.125
I consider jñānī as equal to Myself.

47
00:02:34.125 --> 00:02:37.708
A jñānī's devotion is firm and unbroken,

48
00:02:37.708 --> 00:02:39.333
which binds them

49
00:02:39.333 --> 00:02:42.458
in an unbreakable relationship with Krishna.

50
00:02:42.458 --> 00:02:45.708
Krishna loves all who surrender,

51
00:02:45.708 --> 00:02:48.625
but those who are completely surrendered,

52
00:02:48.625 --> 00:02:50.416
who have considered attaining Krishna

53
00:02:50.416 --> 00:02:52.000
as their very existence,

54
00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:55.166
Krishna gives them a place equal to Himself.

55
00:02:55.166 --> 00:02:58.333
But here it needs to be understood

56
00:02:58.333 --> 00:03:00.416
that its meaning is absolutely not

57
00:03:00.416 --> 00:03:03.000
that that jñānī becomes God.

58
00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:05.625
Lord Krishna's words spoken here

59
00:03:05.625 --> 00:03:10.000
show His intimacy toward that jñānī.

60
00:03:14.583 --> 00:03:16.875
Sorrow and pain,

61
00:03:16.875 --> 00:03:20.416
desire for wealth/property, curiosity,

62
00:03:20.416 --> 00:03:24.625
or complete devotion.

63
00:03:24.625 --> 00:03:27.416
Whatever the reason may be,

64
00:03:27.416 --> 00:03:30.500
one who comes to My shelter,

65
00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:32.541
I accept them.

66
00:03:32.541 --> 00:03:36.041
All are dear to Me.

67
00:03:36.041 --> 00:03:40.458
Most of them may have made this contact

68
00:03:40.458 --> 00:03:45.416
because of desires, but still

69
00:03:45.416 --> 00:03:49.666
they've taken a step toward devotion,

70
00:03:49.666 --> 00:03:54.333
which will bring positive change in their life.

71
00:03:54.333 --> 00:03:56.458
In your personal life too,

72
00:03:56.458 --> 00:04:00.083
people must come to you for help -

73
00:04:00.083 --> 00:04:02.791
some for help in sorrow,

74
00:04:02.791 --> 00:04:07.500
some for your contribution
 in their economic progress,

75
00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:09.583
some carrying curiosity to understand

76
00:04:09.583 --> 00:04:12.791
some subject or perspective,

77
00:04:12.791 --> 00:04:16.458
and some only carrying love.

78
00:04:16.458 --> 00:04:18.750
What kind of behavior

79
00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:21.625
do you maintain with all these?

80
00:04:21.625 --> 00:04:24.750
Most people get irritated with people

81
00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:28.666
who've come to them for some benefit.

82
00:04:28.666 --> 00:04:32.083
This thought immediately comes to mind -

83
00:04:32.083 --> 00:04:33.500
why are these people

84
00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:37.458
wanting something from me?

85
00:04:37.458 --> 00:04:39.500
These people are selfish?

86
00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:41.041
Why should I help,

87
00:04:41.041 --> 00:04:45.000
what will I get in this?

88
00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:48.416
Look by changing perspective a little.

89
00:04:48.416 --> 00:04:51.541
Those people came to you

90
00:04:51.541 --> 00:04:54.000
because you're capable.

91
00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:55.375
And second,

92
00:04:55.375 --> 00:05:00.083
if you yourself want something in return,

93
00:05:00.083 --> 00:05:05.416
then isn't this also selfishness?

94
00:05:05.416 --> 00:05:07.250
You tell me,

95
00:05:07.250 --> 00:05:10.250
if helping someone

96
00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:12.541
isn't causing you harm,

97
00:05:12.541 --> 00:05:15.208
isn't causing harm to anyone else,

98
00:05:15.208 --> 00:05:20.791
then what's the hesitation in helping?

99
00:05:20.791 --> 00:05:23.708
And also think that by helping someone

100
00:05:23.708 --> 00:05:27.791
without selfishness like this,

101
00:05:27.791 --> 00:05:32.625
your mind is also being purified.

102
00:05:32.625 --> 00:05:35.208
Yes, this can definitely happen

103
00:05:35.208 --> 00:05:38.458
that you selflessly helped someone

104
00:05:38.458 --> 00:05:44.000
and they forgot you as soon as work was done.

105
00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:47.000
Don't be disappointed by this.

106
00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:51.250
Because as soon as selfishness
 is fulfilled, forgetting

107
00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:53.125
is their tendency,

108
00:05:53.125 --> 00:05:59.333
but helping as much as possible

109
00:05:59.333 --> 00:06:01.875
is your tendency.

110
00:06:01.875 --> 00:06:05.500
Your appropriate life principles,

111
00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:10.500
don't abandon them because
 of such disappointment.

112
00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:13.791
Now see, you're reading this Gita,

113
00:06:13.791 --> 00:06:15.333
listening to Me,

114
00:06:15.333 --> 00:06:19.333
helping others in every possible way.

115
00:06:19.333 --> 00:06:22.125
So you're connected to two great purposes

116
00:06:22.125 --> 00:06:26.291
of devotion and human welfare.

117
00:06:26.291 --> 00:06:31.708
For this reason, you're
 also extremely dear to Me.

118
00:06:31.708 --> 00:06:37.041
You just keep walking on the path of goodness,

119
00:06:37.041 --> 00:06:41.166
I am always with you.

120
00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:49.708
Many people come to My shelter.

121
00:06:49.708 --> 00:06:53.166
Everyone's level of devotion is different -

122
00:06:53.166 --> 00:06:56.541
someone remembers only in sorrow,

123
00:06:56.541 --> 00:06:59.583
someone for economic prosperity, someone

124
00:06:59.583 --> 00:07:03.500
because of curiosity, and
 someone only because of love

125
00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:06.166
and devotion.

126
00:07:06.166 --> 00:07:09.791
All are dear to Me.

127
00:07:09.791 --> 00:07:13.375
In the family too, there are many people.

128
00:07:13.375 --> 00:07:16.916
Whether success or understanding of life,

129
00:07:16.916 --> 00:07:19.875
everyone will be at different levels.

130
00:07:19.875 --> 00:07:21.291
But

131
00:07:21.291 --> 00:07:24.208
the family is one, right?

132
00:07:24.208 --> 00:07:26.875
Everyone has to stay together.

133
00:07:26.875 --> 00:07:29.333
But many times family elders

134
00:07:29.333 --> 00:07:33.041
start comparing younger ones with each other.

135
00:07:33.041 --> 00:07:35.166
Start criticizing one

136
00:07:35.166 --> 00:07:38.750
while considering another dear.

137
00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:42.291
Make the mistake of discouraging others

138
00:07:42.291 --> 00:07:46.875
by giving example of one who moved ahead.

139
00:07:46.875 --> 00:07:48.833
Everyone having different progress,

140
00:07:48.833 --> 00:07:51.833
different pace is natural, right?

141
00:07:51.833 --> 00:07:54.625
Then why this favoritism?

142
00:07:54.625 --> 00:07:58.875
And this very favoritism
 sometimes weakens the family,

143
00:07:58.875 --> 00:08:02.291
creates mutual discord and jealousy.

144
00:08:02.291 --> 00:08:04.791
And as a family elder,

145
00:08:04.791 --> 00:08:07.583
if your love for a family member,

146
00:08:07.583 --> 00:08:11.208
for a younger one depends on their success,

147
00:08:11.208 --> 00:08:12.708
then

148
00:08:12.708 --> 00:08:14.791
isn't this inappropriate?

149
00:08:14.791 --> 00:08:16.750
When you were small

150
00:08:16.750 --> 00:08:20.208
and there were other people
 of your age in the family,

151
00:08:20.208 --> 00:08:24.416
was everyone's progress equal?

152
00:08:24.416 --> 00:08:25.500
No, right?

153
00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:27.958
So in such a case, what did you want?

154
00:08:27.958 --> 00:08:30.875
Encouragement or criticism?

155
00:08:30.875 --> 00:08:33.333
When someone makes a mistake,
 definitely teach them.

156
00:08:33.333 --> 00:08:36.666
Definitely show them the path for progress.

157
00:08:36.666 --> 00:08:39.041
But keep this in mind

158
00:08:39.041 --> 00:08:42.833
that no one learns from only criticism.

159
00:08:42.833 --> 00:08:47.541
And also remember that everyone
 has some quality or other,

160
00:08:47.541 --> 00:08:51.833
and appreciating those qualities
 is also extremely necessary.

161
00:08:51.833 --> 00:08:55.375
When life's lessons of progress
 are given positively,

162
00:08:55.375 --> 00:08:56.958
without criticism

163
00:08:56.958 --> 00:09:00.791
and with proper appreciation,

164
00:09:00.791 --> 00:09:04.291
only then are they most effective.

165
00:09:04.291 --> 00:09:06.000
Keep this matter in mind,

166
00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:06.958
and yes,

167
00:09:06.958 --> 00:09:09.875
there's no place for favoritism in the family.

168
00:09:09.875 --> 00:09:12.208
Don't forget this either.

169
00:09:12.208 --> 00:09:15.000
If you're the elder of the family,

170
00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:17.833
then you're the root of that family.

171
00:09:17.833 --> 00:09:21.291
If you'll create flow of positivity,

172
00:09:21.291 --> 00:09:25.083
then the tree in the form of family
 will always remain strong.

173
00:09:25.083 --> 00:09:27.541
Will blossom with love.

174
00:09:27.541 --> 00:09:30.291
Do think about this matter.

175
00:09:34.708 --> 00:09:38.250
Whichever devotee comes to My shelter,

176
00:09:38.250 --> 00:09:41.000
they're acceptable to Me,

177
00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:43.958
I will help them.

178
00:09:43.958 --> 00:09:47.791
All are dear to Me,

179
00:09:47.791 --> 00:09:50.875
and My effort is this -

180
00:09:50.875 --> 00:09:53.583
that I encourage everyone

181
00:09:53.583 --> 00:09:57.083
to reach the level of jñānī

182
00:09:57.083 --> 00:10:01.250
and know spirituality's supreme truth.

183
00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:03.291
Attain Me.

184
00:10:03.291 --> 00:10:06.458
Yes, their spiritual progress will definitely

185
00:10:06.458 --> 00:10:10.208
be determined by their own effort, but

186
00:10:10.208 --> 00:10:11.000
in My heart

187
00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:14.750
there are good wishes of progress for all.

188
00:10:14.750 --> 00:10:16.583
In the business field,

189
00:10:16.583 --> 00:10:19.250
if you're in some senior position,

190
00:10:19.250 --> 00:10:20.458
then understanding this matter

191
00:10:20.458 --> 00:10:21.500
is extremely

192
00:10:21.500 --> 00:10:25.583
necessary for you - that all
 people working under you

193
00:10:25.583 --> 00:10:29.416
will be of different personalities,

194
00:10:29.416 --> 00:10:32.083
their judgment will be different,

195
00:10:32.083 --> 00:10:34.000
work skill will be different.

196
00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:38.291
And yes, their purposes will also be different -

197
00:10:38.291 --> 00:10:40.916
someone is desirous of continuously learning,

198
00:10:40.916 --> 00:10:43.833
someone's goal is personal progress,

199
00:10:43.833 --> 00:10:47.666
whereas someone else, because
 of life's compulsions,

200
00:10:47.666 --> 00:10:51.083
is doing this work for livelihood.

201
00:10:51.083 --> 00:10:54.666
Everyone is on their own different life journey.

202
00:10:54.666 --> 00:10:59.333
As a senior and wise officer,

203
00:10:59.333 --> 00:11:01.500
your responsibility becomes

204
00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:05.666
to keep respect for everyone in the mind.

205
00:11:05.666 --> 00:11:07.791
Don't scorn anyone.

206
00:11:07.791 --> 00:11:10.333
Whatever the purposes may be,

207
00:11:10.333 --> 00:11:13.166
accept everyone.

208
00:11:13.166 --> 00:11:15.208
After that,

209
00:11:15.208 --> 00:11:17.250
you'll also have to 

210
00:11:17.250 --> 00:11:18.500
encourage everyone

211
00:11:18.500 --> 00:11:22.500
according to their level and purpose.

212
00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:24.166
For example - one who is struggling

213
00:11:24.166 --> 00:11:27.458
with life's compulsions,

214
00:11:27.458 --> 00:11:31.416
they won't be as attracted to obtaining knowledge

215
00:11:31.416 --> 00:11:32.416
as

216
00:11:32.416 --> 00:11:35.875
from the perspective of economic progress.

217
00:11:35.875 --> 00:11:38.000
And there will also be some people

218
00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:41.666
who are extremely wise, hardworking,

219
00:11:41.666 --> 00:11:46.166
also have the capability to reach your level.

220
00:11:46.166 --> 00:11:48.500
Some senior officers feel

221
00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:51.500
insecure from this,

222
00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:53.750
and forget

223
00:11:53.750 --> 00:11:57.958
that their progress also happened like this.

224
00:11:57.958 --> 00:12:01.625
So instead of feeling insecure,

225
00:12:01.625 --> 00:12:04.125
you also make your progress.

226
00:12:04.125 --> 00:12:05.208
Rather, from this thing,

227
00:12:05.208 --> 00:12:06.083
a senior

228
00:12:06.083 --> 00:12:08.750
officer should be pleased

229
00:12:08.750 --> 00:12:11.916
that people working under them

230
00:12:11.916 --> 00:12:14.541
are progressing.

231
00:12:14.541 --> 00:12:16.333
Just as I give

232
00:12:16.333 --> 00:12:23.416
My devotees protection and inspiration for
 progress according to their situation,

233
00:12:23.416 --> 00:12:30.416
similarly you too must become such
 an officer for your colleagues

234
00:12:30.416 --> 00:12:32.458
who gives them protection,

235
00:12:32.458 --> 00:12:34.750
is desirous of their progress,

236
00:12:34.750 --> 00:12:37.041
helps them.

237
00:12:37.041 --> 00:12:41.000
This is the mark of true leadership, right?
